The '''Well-being Fund of Sanyan''' ({{langx|kz|ߏߥߏ-ߊߘߐ ߊߟߊߊߝߌߊ|Owó-àpò Àlàáfíà|well-being money purse}}) is the [[W:Sovereign wealth fund|sovereign wealth fund]] collective owned by the [[government of Sanyan]]. It consists of two entirely separate sovereign wealth funds: the Well-being Fund Global and the Sanyanian Pension Fund.

The '''Well-being Fund Global''' (''Àlàáfíà Owó-àpò Àgbáyé''), also known as the Oil Fund (''Èpò Owó-àpò''), was established in 1948 following the [[Sanyan Emergency]] to invest the surplus revenues of the Sanyanian [[W:Petroleum industry|petroleum sector]] (dominated by the state-owned [[Kafauco]]). {{asof|August 2025|post=,}} it had over ε1.002 trillion in assets, equal to 0.x% of the value of the world's listed companies, making it the world's seventh-largest [[W:Sovereign wealth fund|sovereign wealth fund]] in terms of total [[W:Assets under management|assets under management]]. It also holds [[portfolio (finance)|portfolios]] of real estate and fixed-income investments. Many companies are excluded by the fund on [[W:Socially responsible investing|ethical grounds]] (see [[Sanyan#Resources]]).

